-- Two PVT regions in a compositional run.  A row of 30 cells holds oil of three
-- components (CO2, methane, decane) and water.  Cells 1-15 are in PVT region 1
-- with fresh water (PVTW and DENSITY: 1000 kg/m3 at surface, 0.3 cP) and cells
-- 16-30 in region 2 with brine (1150 kg/m3 at surface, 0.9 cP).  There are no
-- wells: region 1 starts at 170 bar and region 2 at 130 bar, so oil and water
-- flow into region 2 until the pressure evens out.
--
-- Each cell takes the water properties of its own PVT region.  The water in
-- cells 16-30 has the density and viscosity of the brine, about 1140 kg/m3 and
-- 0.9 cP, and the water in cells 1-15 those of the fresh water, about 975 kg/m3
-- and 0.3 cP.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   COMPOSITIONAL TWO PVT REGIONS

METRIC

TABDIMS
1* 2 /
OIL
GAS
WATER
DIMENS
30 1 1
/

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP /

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

------------------------------------------------------------------------
